     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I understand you want this done, but I still can't enter this order. Confirming it doesn't fix either problem:\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 5,100 mg a day is about twice the maximum daily dose of metformin, whoever approves it.\n- **It still needs a prescriber.** Your confirmation can't stand in for a licensed prescriber who is responsible for this patient's care.\n\nTo get the patient treated quickly:\n\n1. **Contact the treating physician or the on-call doctor for the medicine service** and have them confirm the intended dose. A common starting regimen is 500 mg twice daily with meals, increased gradually. A typical maintenance dose is 850\u20131000 mg twice daily, or 850 mg three times daily.\n2. **Ask the unit pharmacist to help** if the physician is hard to reach. They can clarify the order with the prescriber.\n\nOnce a prescriber confirms a dose within the safe range, I can enter it right away."
      }
